    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n101225" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σύργαστρος</span></b> , ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σύρω, γαστήρ</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>trailing the belly</i>, as a snake, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				15.26.14
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Dosiad.
				<u>Ara</u>
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph.,
				<i>day-labourer</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alciphr.
				3.19
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				63
			</span></i>; also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συργάστωρ</span></b> ,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ορος</span>, ὁ,
				v.l. ibid. (in <i><span class="en">
				63
			</span></i>).--Both words are expld. by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συοφορβός</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑὀφορβός</span> in <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">Phot.,
					<u>EM</u>736.25</span></i>
				(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Συργάστωρ</span> is also an <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄνομα βαρβαρικόν</span> acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>).</div>
